    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d396">

                <pb facs="0712" n="576" xml:id="pg576"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.79625/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-08-03T19:00:00-05:00">August 3, 1929—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:30 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>147. Responsive to the message your telegram No. 79, July 31, 6 p.m., instructed
                    me to convey, President Leguía authorized me to inform President Hoover and
                    yourself that he was entirely of your opinion respecting the proposed
                    conference. He will inform the Chilean Government that because of Peru’s
                    aviation commitments the Peruvian Government is not free to participate in the
                    proposed conference.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
